Z||000005||formula2||08-25-2001||11:24 PM||||BTW front grille are easy to change butI can't take out the back grille .What is the best way to do it??<BR>Thank's||||reg||5
Z||000006||8Ball||08-26-2001||03:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by formula2:<BR><B>BTW front grille are easy to change butI can't take out the back grille .What is the best way to do it??<BR>Thank's</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well you could do like me, Hit a speed bump Rather fast, The impact of the bump knocked off both back grills and the rearview mirror  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Who on earth thought it was a good idea to put a speed bump right after a blind curve!!!<P>no telling what else I did to the poor car.||||reg||1
Z||000007||gargoyle||08-26-2001||04:35 AM||||OWCH!!!! That must have hurt.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>I think that the red in the mats might be a good idea. Keeping things small, what about a set of the door emblems that Oreif has in red also. Just enough but not too much.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by gargoyle (edited 08-26-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000008||Monkeyman||08-26-2001||08:53 AM||||There are a couple of ways you can remove the rear speaker grills.  One, you can just rip them off, but you'll be taking the chance of breaking the trim.  Or two, you can remove the trim (I did it this way as I had to recover the headliner anyway) and drill out the plastic rivit things.  It seems that the rear grills are made with 4 "tabs" that fit through the trim.  Once they're through, Pontiac used heat to mushroom the ends.  I plan to use some silicone to reattach mine.  I don't use the speakers anyway.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||08-26-2001||08:56 AM||||I have a nice steering wheel in red and black on ebay real cheap that is new and would match them. really well.<BR><A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=594730346" TARGET=_blank>Click here to check it out</A><BR>Looks good by the way<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
