Z||000015||Springtyme||08-27-2001||12:00 PM||||You just painted them? They look pretty sweet! How easy was it? I might paint mine.... =)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> <P>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||14
Z||000016||Ryan Wright||08-27-2001||12:02 PM||||MD: No paint. I bought new speaker grille cloth that was already red and recovered them. You can buy white grille cloth almost anywhere. Check your local audio shops. Recovering is easy: Pull the old stuff off (it's glued on), cut out a piece slightly bigger than what you need, and start gluing it on one side at a time. Do one of the longer sides, then the two edges. Pull & stretch the fabric a little as you glue it on, so it stays nice and tight. I used the gel based superglue; the liquid stuff is too runny. I'm sure other types of glue would work as well, but the superglue sets up quickly. Buy a few packages. I used two tubes per grille.<P>I wouldn't paint them. If you were careful you could probably make them look decent with paint, but it would clog things up and your speakers would sound horrible. Likewise, don't just use regular old fabric. It will do the same thing. Speaker grille cloth is available all over the Internet, and at most local audio shops. Speciality colors are hard to find. I had to go all over town to find it in red, and finally came across a nice fabric store that had it in a variety of colors. The fabric store didn't call it grille cloth, it had some other name which I forget, but it's almost the same stuff. If you stretch it (it should be slightly elastic), you should be able to see through it somewhat.<P>------------------<BR>-Ryan Wright (http://www.ryanwright.com)<p>[This message has been edited by Ryan Wright (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Ryan Wright||08-27-2001||12:12 PM||||I should also add that you can have them dyed any color you want. First, you recover your grilles in white. Then take them down to an upholstery shop and have them dyed. Don't dye the cloth before putting it on: The dye will cause the cloth to lose it's elasticity, and you will have a hard time getting a nice tight fit.<P>------------------<BR>-Ryan Wright (http://www.ryanwright.com)||||reg||1
Z||000018||Oreif||08-27-2001||12:38 PM||||The door tabs come in any color combination you want. Here are an example of some of the different styles I can do. They cost $5.00.<BR>Just Email me at:<BR>se1986@home.com<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Emblems_2.jpg">   <BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
